        <div class="BI_termBanner">
      <div class="pdph1"><h1>ULIP Charges</h1></div>
      <p class="pdpBanner_desc">
        <p>ULIP charges are the fees incurred for managing the investment and insurance components of a Unit Linked Insurance Plan. Since a ULIP plan combines financial protection and wealth creation, a number of charges are deducted from the premium paid to manage the plan. Some common examples include: premium allocation charges, fund management charges, policy administration charges, mortality charges, and other applicable fees. These charges affect the amount invested and the overall returns generated by the policy. A proper understanding of these charges helps you make an informed investment decision.</p>

